    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0539" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/638: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-06T08:00:00-00:44">December 6, 1929—8
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s circular telegram dated December 1, 4 p.m., complied with yesterday.
                        Barclay<anchor n="72" xml:id="d340-f1"/> states that Liberia will support
                    Pact of Paris and intend[s] to issue similar statement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d340-f1" n="72" xml:id="d340-f1-content">
                <p>Edwin Barclay, Liberian Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
